Subject: macOS: msync MRING wait-path tracer (temporary)

Lock-free ring recording which msync objects each thread is about to block on,
snapshotted to /tmp/mring_<pid>.log by a background thread. Enabled with
WINE_MRING=1.

It exists to find a lost wakeup that fprintf-based tracing perturbs away: the
TRACE path's latency reorders the sub-microsecond race out of existence, so the
tracer has to cost one atomic fetch-add and a few plain stores on the hot path.

Kept as its own patch rather than folded into 0008 so it can be dropped in one
move when the investigation it serves is finished.

